From c961b4020c4b9ae8e07c5a4c4d6b18983861b67c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen LeBLanc <stpleb@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:42:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PortableTAK: federation RabbitMQ bridge reopens connections
 the broker closed

The inbound publisher connection sits idle between federated events, so
RabbitMQ closes it after missed heartbeats; the next inbound event raised
StreamLostError and dropped the whole federation link for 30 s (events sent
in that gap were lost). Publisher retries once on a fresh connection; the
outbound consumer reopens instead of silently stopping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
